Acceptance Criteria
Unique Daily Images:
o    Each day, players see exactly five unique images from the image bank.
o    Images displayed are not repeated from previous days until the full set has been cycled.
Image Collection and Location Logging:
o    10 unique images are captured from different locations around campus.
o    Each image is tagged with its location to validate correct answers.
Smooth Transition Between Images:
o    Transition animations are implemented between images to ensure a seamless experience.
o    Transitions are tested to confirm smoothness on different devices (if applicable).
Image Bank Management:
o    Images are stored in a database or storage solution with metadata (e.g., location, ID).
o    Images displayed each day are marked to prevent duplication within the same session.
Random Image Selection:
o    The game’s randomizer successfully selects five unique images each day from the image bank.
o    Testing confirms the randomizer does not repeat images within the same day.
Multiple-Choice Layout:
o    Four answer options are displayed below each image, formatted for clear visibility.
o    Options are randomized to prevent players from guessing based on option placement.
Unique Answer Options:
o    Each multiple-choice question has four unique answers without duplicates.
o    Testing confirms no duplicate answers appear in a single question set.
Single Guess Validation:
o    Players are restricted to only one guess per image.
o    If a player attempts multiple guesses, an error message or visual feedback indicates only one guess is allowed.
Error Handling:
o    Proper error handling is implemented for cases such as missing images, loading issues, or repeated answers.
o    Errors are communicated to players through messages or indicators to improve user experience.
